  "reason": "Evidence: The top configuration (config_029, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. RNA encoder choice has been the most impactful variable (scvi_n200 at 0.725 vs scgpt at 0.520), but pca_n2000—a linear, non-learned dimensionality reduction—has not been tested in any multimodal setting. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the learned latent space of scvi_n200 is truly necessary or whether a simpler linear projection (pca_n2000) could perform comparably when paired with the strong image encoder and transformer aggregation. This experiment isolically tests the RNA encoder variable within the best-known architecture (multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted), making it a clean single-factor comparison to config_029. If pca_n2000 matches or approaches scvi_n200, it reveals the RNA signal is relatively low-dimensional and the architecture is robust; if it falls well below, it confirms the learned representation is essential and focuses remaining budget on image-encoder or profile-setting refinements. With 3 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information experiment to either confirm or rule out a major design axis before final exploitation."
